              "name": "Universal Physics Transformer (UPT)",
              "protocol_description": "UPTs operate without grid- or particle-based latent structures, using a fixed number of latent tokens. They encode input states into a latent representation, propagate dynamics in latent space via an approximator, and decode at any query point. Training uses inverse encoding (reconstructing input from latent) and inverse decoding (reconstructing latent from output) losses to isolate encoder, approximator, and decoder responsibilities."
